              "details": "Previously, after a channel has been established, a malicious peer could send crafted messages that would deadlock the entire connection.\n\nNow, we handle all RFC 4254 channel messages; global requests are handled explicitly. Then, treat all other messages as a protocol error and tear the connection down instead of buffering and blocking.",
              "id": "GO-2026-6355",
              "modified": "2026-09-03T10:10:55.101133330Z",
              "published": "2026-09-02T19:12:04Z",
